{% comment %}The Theme setting: dark paints this plugin's own view, never the rest of a mashup.{% endcomment %}
{% assign theme = trmnl.plugin_settings.custom_fields_values.theme %}
{% if theme == "dark" %}{% assign dark_classes = "inverse bg--canvas " %}{% endif %}
{% if has_race and race %}
{% assign full_news_size = "title--base lg:title--large" %}
{% if news.size > 6 %}{% assign full_news_size = "title--small lg:title--base" %}{% endif %}
<div class="{{ dark_classes }}layout layout--col layout--top layout--stretch-x gap--medium">
  <div class="flex flex--row flex--center-y gap--medium">
    <div class="grow">
      {% render "race_header", race: race, name_size: "title--large portrait:title--small lg:text--xxxlarge lg:portrait:text--xlarge", detail_size: "label--base portrait:label--small lg:label--xlarge lg:portrait:label--large", flag_size: "h--[56px] w--max-[112px] lg:h--[96px] lg:w--max-48", compact_details: true, theme: theme %}
    </div>
    <div class="flex-none">{% render "qr", url: race.url, size_class: "w--[56px] h--[56px] lg:w--[96px] lg:h--[96px]" %}</div>
  </div>
  {% comment %}
    Two columns side by side, stacked in portrait: side by side on a portrait
    X they squeezed every name and time onto two lines and left the bottom
    half empty.
  {% endcomment %}
  {% if race_finished %}
  {% comment %}
    The weekend is over, so the timeline goes: the winner, the latest news
    and when the next round is on the left; the whole classification on the
    right. On the landscape X, h--0 with grow fixes the remaining height
    before overflow measures the news; otherwise the grid expands to fit it
    and the next race ends up under the title bar (seen on a device on
    11 October 2026, after a TRMNL sync had reverted this). Portrait keeps
    its natural height for the classification below. The landscape X splits
    7:5 (measured 12 October 2026 at 1872px: the wider classification table
    needs 330px for "P1 HAM 1:42:00.785" and gets 373, the other needs 303
    and gets 312, so nothing wraps; 8:4 would wrap the winner's time). Half
    and half, most headlines wrapped onto two lines. The OG stays equal
    halves: at two fifths of its 800px the gap column wrapped "+1 lap". The
    winner's name fits either column through value fitting.
  {% endcomment %}
  <div class="grid grid--cols-2 portrait:grid--cols-1 lg:landscape:grid--cols-12 gap--large grow lg:h--0 lg:portrait:h--auto">
    <div class="flex flex--col flex--stretch-x gap--medium lg:landscape:col--span-7">
      <div class="flex flex--col flex--center gap--xsmall">
        {% comment %}"Race winner" a step below the build-up's lead label on the X, for a fifth headline.{% endcomment %}
        {% render "lead", lead: lead, size: "value--large lg:value--xxlarge", label_size: "lg:title--xlarge" %}
      </div>
      {% render "checker" %}
      {% if news.size > 0 %}
      <div class="grow lg:h--0 lg:portrait:h--auto">
        <div class="lg:hidden portrait:hidden">{% render "news", news: news, limit: 3, headline_size: "title--small" %}</div>
        <div class="hidden portrait:block lg:portrait:hidden">{% render "news", news: news, limit: 3, headline_size: "title--small" %}</div>
        {% comment %}On the landscape X, offer every headline to the overflow engine in the height left above the next race.{% endcomment %}
        <div class="hidden lg:block lg:portrait:hidden h--full">{% render "news", news: news, limit: 20, headline_size: "lg:title--base", fill: true %}</div>
        <div class="hidden lg:portrait:block">{% render "news", news: news, limit: 3, headline_size: "lg:title--base" %}</div>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
      {% if next_race %}{% render "next_race", next_race: next_race, theme: theme %}{% endif %}
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex--col flex--stretch-x flex--center-y h--full portrait:h--auto lg:landscape:col--span-5">
      <div class="portrait:hidden">{% render "classification", result: result, size: "table--xsmall lg:table--base" %}</div>
      <div class="hidden portrait:block">{% render "classification", result: result, size: "table--xsmall lg:table--small" %}</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  {% else %}
  <div class="grid grid--cols-2 portrait:grid--cols-1 gap--large grow">
    <div class="flex flex--col flex--stretch-x gap--auto">
      {% if between_rounds and upcoming.size > 0 %}
        <div class="portrait:hidden">{% render "upcoming", upcoming: upcoming, limit: 3, size: "table--small lg:table--large", title_size: "lg:title--large" %}</div>
        <div class="hidden portrait:block">{% render "upcoming", upcoming: upcoming, limit: 5, size: "table--small lg:table--large", title_size: "lg:title--large" %}</div>
      {% else %}
      <div class="flex flex--col flex--center gap--xsmall">
        {% render "lead", lead: lead, size: "value--large lg:value--xxlarge", label_size: "lg:text--mega" %}
        {% comment %}Stacked on the X: on one line a long forecast ("Thunderstorms", gusts) overran the column at this size.{% endcomment %}
        {% render "lead_weather", weather: lead.weather, text_size: "lg:label--xlarge", stack: "lg:", theme: theme %}
      </div>
      {% endif %}
      {% render "checker" %}
      {% comment %}No weather line: each timeline row carries its own forecast.{% endcomment %}
      {% comment %}The forecast a step smaller in the landscape X's half-width column: at `label--large` a sprint weekend's row ran past it.{% endcomment %}
      {% comment %}
        A whole qualifying field stacked below on the portrait X ran under the
        title bar at P19, and the race-morning grid lost P11 and P22: the
        timeline keeps its last three rows there. Two `if`s, because Liquid
        reads `a and b or c` as `a and (b or c)`.
      {% endcomment %}
      {% assign short_timeline = false %}
      {% if focus == "result" and result.rows.size > 10 %}{% assign short_timeline = true %}{% endif %}
      {% if focus == "grid" %}{% assign short_timeline = true %}{% endif %}
      {% if short_timeline %}
      <div class="lg:portrait:hidden">{% render "schedule", schedule: schedule, size: "table--small lg:table--large", name: "label", aligned: true, fill: true, forecast_size: "lg:label--base lg:portrait:label--large", no_next: between_rounds, theme: theme %}</div>
      <div class="hidden lg:portrait:block">{% render "schedule", schedule: schedule, limit: 3, tail: true, size: "table--small lg:table--large", name: "label", aligned: true, fill: true, forecast_size: "lg:label--base lg:portrait:label--large", no_next: between_rounds, theme: theme %}</div>
      {% else %}
      {% render "schedule", schedule: schedule, size: "table--small lg:table--large", name: "label", aligned: true, fill: true, forecast_size: "lg:label--base lg:portrait:label--large", no_next: between_rounds, theme: theme %}
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex--col flex--stretch-x gap--small h--full">
      {% comment %}
        The focus block takes the column's spare height. TRMNL's overflow
        script hides news items that do not fit, and a separate spacer would
        read to it as content.
      {% endcomment %}
      <div class="grow {% if focus == 'standings' or focus == 'result' and news.size == 0 %}flex flex--col flex--stretch-x flex--center-y h--full{% elsif focus == 'grid' or focus == 'result' %}flex flex--col flex--stretch-x gap--medium lg:gap--small h--full{% elsif news.size == 0 %}h--full{% endif %}">
        {% if focus == "result" %}
          {% comment %}
            The whole field in two columns with times, as the race reads once
            it is over: a qualifying result is tomorrow's grid, unless a grid
            has been published, which takes this place instead. Stacked under
            the timeline in portrait, where eleven rows a column need the
            compact height on the X too.
          {% endcomment %}
          <div class="portrait:hidden">{% render "classification", result: result, size: "table--xsmall lg:table--base" %}</div>
          <div class="hidden portrait:block">{% render "classification", result: result, size: "table--xsmall" %}</div>
          {% comment %}
            Headlines under the classification, as under the grid: it was
            centred in the column with the space above and below it unused.
            Not on a portrait OG, where the field stacks under the timeline
            and a headline ran under the title bar. On the landscape X the
            headline is a full-width row under both columns instead (below).
          {% endcomment %}
          {% if news.size > 0 %}
          <div class="grow lg:hidden portrait:hidden">{% render "news", news: news, limit: 2, headline_size: "title--small", clamp: 1, fill: true %}</div>
          <div class="grow hidden lg:portrait:block">{% render "news", news: news, limit: 1, headline_size: "title--base", clamp: 1, strict_clamp: true, fill: true %}</div>
          {% endif %}
        {% elsif focus == "standings" %}
          {% comment %}Stacked under the timeline in portrait, where the full width takes four columns.{% endcomment %}
          <div class="portrait:hidden">{% render "championship", rows: standings.drivers, cols: 2, size: "table--xsmall lg:table--base" %}</div>
          <div class="hidden portrait:block">{% render "championship", rows: standings.drivers, cols: 4, size: "table--xsmall lg:table--small" %}</div>
        {% elsif focus == "grid" %}
          {% render "grid", grid: grid %}
          {% comment %}
            Keep two one-line headlines on the OG and one two-line headline
            on the X. The tighter X gap above the news reserves both lines
            below all 22 grid places, including in portrait.
          {% endcomment %}
          {% if grid_news.size > 0 %}
          <div class="grow lg:hidden">{% render "news", news: grid_news, limit: 2, headline_size: "title--small", clamp: 1, fill: true %}</div>
          <div class="grow hidden lg:block">{% render "news", news: grid_news, limit: 1, headline_size: "title--base", clamp: 2, strict_clamp: true, fill: true %}</div>
          {% endif %}
        {% elsif focus == "news" %}
          {% comment %}
            Cap headlines for the physical screen size. The overflow script
            left the last two-line item partly under the title bar on the OG.
          {% endcomment %}
          <div class="grow lg:hidden">
            {% render "news", news: news, limit: 7, headline_size: full_news_size, fill: true, empty_size: "lg:label--large" %}
          </div>
          <div class="grow hidden lg:block lg:portrait:hidden">
            {% render "news", news: news, limit: 11, headline_size: full_news_size, fill: true, empty_size: "lg:label--large" %}
          </div>
          <div class="grow hidden lg:portrait:block">
            {% render "news", news: news, limit: 10, headline_size: full_news_size, fill: true, empty_size: "lg:label--large" %}
          </div>
        {% elsif news.size == 0 %}
          {% render "news", news: news, limit: 1, headline_size: full_news_size, fill: true, empty_size: "lg:label--large" %}
        {% endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  {% comment %}
    A qualifying result on the landscape X: the headline runs the full width
    under both columns. Inside the result column it was cut off at half the
    screen, beside timeline rows spread out to fill the height.
  {% endcomment %}
  {% if focus == "result" and news.size > 0 %}
  <div class="hidden lg:block lg:portrait:hidden">{% render "news", news: news, limit: 1, headline_size: "title--base", clamp: 1, strict_clamp: true %}</div>
  {% endif %}
  {% endif %}
</div>
{% elsif standings %}
{% comment %}
  The off-season: 22 drivers in two columns, and all 11 constructors in the
  third. One headline and the QR code sit beside the heading so neither can
  be pushed below the screen by the tables. In portrait, constructors follow
  the drivers.
{% endcomment %}
<div class="{{ dark_classes }}layout layout--col layout--top layout--stretch-x gap--small">
  <div class="flex flex--row flex--center-y gap--medium portrait:hidden">
    <div class="grow flex flex--col flex--left flex--stretch-x gap--small">
      {% render "standings_header", standings: standings, title_size: "lg:title--xlarge", detail_size: "lg:label--large" %}
      {% render "news", news: news, limit: 1, headline_size: "title--small lg:title--base" %}
    </div>
    {% render "qr", url: standings.url %}
  </div>
  <div class="hidden portrait:block">
    <div class="flex flex--row flex--center-y gap--small">
      <div class="grow">{% render "standings_header", standings: standings, title_size: "lg:title--xlarge", detail_size: "lg:label--large" %}</div>
      <div class="flex-none">{% render "qr", url: standings.url %}</div>
    </div>
    {% if news.size > 0 %}{% render "news", news: news, limit: 1, headline_size: "title--small lg:title--base" %}{% endif %}
  </div>
  <div class="grid grid--cols-3 portrait:grid--cols-2 gap--medium grow">
    <div class="flex flex--col flex--stretch-x flex--center-y gap--xsmall col--span-2">
      <span class="title title--small lg:title--base">Drivers</span>
      <div class="grid grid--cols-2 gap--medium">
        {% assign drivers_half = standings.drivers.size | plus: 1 | divided_by: 2 %}
        {% render "standings_table", label: "", rows: standings.drivers, limit: drivers_half, offset: 0, size: "table--xsmall lg:table--base lg:portrait:table--small" %}
        {% render "standings_table", label: "", rows: standings.drivers, limit: drivers_half, offset: drivers_half, size: "table--xsmall lg:table--base lg:portrait:table--small" %}
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex--col flex--stretch-x flex--center-y h--full">
      {% render "standings_table", label: "Constructors", rows: standings.constructors, limit: 11, offset: 0, size: "table--xsmall lg:table--base lg:portrait:table--small" %}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
{% else %}
<div class="{{ dark_classes }}layout layout--col layout--center">
  <span class="title">No race scheduled.</span>
</div>
{% endif %}
{% render "title_bar", race: race, theme: theme %}
